{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510122-bsd-experimental-pack","id":1510122,"title":"BSD Experimental Pack","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-29T14:14:02-07:00","id":1510122,"title":"BSD Experimental Pack","content":"Think of it as an exercise if you like. I was, for reasons, thinking of a pack/caern formation where there would be a BSD originally from every tribe of garou in existence or they would be a manifestation or result of the worst of the tribe, however they would have to have a reason to migrate from one tribe to the other, naturally, and like, I had a block while I was thinking through some possible scenarios and so I wanted opinions if anyone has. I already have ideas that I believe are functional enough for the Silver Fangs; Bone Gnawers; Red Talons and Black Furies the rest I was kind of unsure or just clueless so I wanted ideas if anyone has any.<br /> <br /> I actually also had ideas on how to use the, Shadow Lords, Glass Walkers and GoF, but I don't know if they turned out good enough so second opinions would be nice.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T15:18:12-07:00","id":1510130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510122-bsd-experimental-pack#post1510122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...however they would have to have a reason to migrate from one tribe to the other...\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really confusing me as to what you're looking for help on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T16:38:13-07:00","id":1510132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510122-bsd-experimental-pack?p=1510130#post1510130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is really confusing me as to what you're looking for help on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there was a translation problem. I'm saying they would need a reason to leave the tribe and join BSD, I could just say they were mistreated or that they are metis or just forced to dance the spiral which would be pretty easy and even works, but I wanted something more developed, understand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T17:11:43-07:00","id":1510136,"title":"","content":"Shadow Lords: This feels like kinda low hanging fruit because they're already the manipulative bastard Tribe and generally upset that the Silver Fangs get all the respect in the Garou Nation. Resentment is a really start to a more developed story for why one would switch sides. If you want something a bit less obvious, a Child of Bat that ends up following Bat into the Wyrm's arms instead of bringing Bat back to Gaia is a more tragic background.<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers: The purge of the Cyberdogs is a pretty easy option, as the BSDs would gladly welcome an unethical cybernetics expert that cares more about continuing their work than patient consent. The torment they could inflict without having to hide what they're doing from their compatriots easily reflects the Wyrm's love of twisting the tools of the Weaver into things of pain and corruption.<br /> <br /> Get of Fenris: Again you have the purge of the Swords of Heimdall to draw on as an easy source of Fenrir that might fall to the Wyrm with something a bit more nuanced than one of the most violent and bloodthirsty Tribes repeating what the White Howlers did.<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia: I don't really like the Bringers of Eternal Peace, but they're the extension of the Tribe that's a natural fit for this. Deciding that the way to fix the world is to just make the Apocalypse happen ASAP makes them ripe to fall to the Wyrm in full. Anything else is probably going to feel like an awkward fit for being in the Tribe to fall later, or just too simplistic like the number of angry Crinos-born in the Tribe as it is.<br /> <br /> Fianna: A lot of overlap with the Fenrir here really; or the Red Talons via the Children of Dire and Mother's Fundamentalists. The difficulty of something that's uniquely Fianna and deeper than some of the more universal things that can drive a Garou to the Spiral is one of the detriments of the Tribe. Like my example of the Child of Bat and the Shadow Lords, the Fianna do have a lot of guilt around what happened to the White Howlers and Lion, leaving a story of seeking to help repair the past taking someone down into dark places they don't come back from and still be on the side they started on.<br /> <br /> Silent Striders: Like the Bone Gnawers that have a continual cannibalism problem that leads many of their members astray. The Followers of Set and the Bane Mummies represent foes that would delight in bringing a Strider to the Wyrm. For something more personal, the Striders' close link to death means one can easily be haunted by their actions quite literally, driving them towards fatalistic options after too long fighting a losing war.<br /> <br /> Stargazers: Basically the same issues as the Children of Gaia.<br /> <br /> Older and Younger Brother: The &quot;we gave everyone evil Camps&quot; adds the obvious story hooks here. Both Tribes have lingering resentment over the European conquest of the Americas, and members willing to deal with the Wyrm's servants to enact some revenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T18:16:39-07:00","id":1510137,"title":"","content":"I actually wanted something more individual and personal for each one to disband.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510122-bsd-experimental-pack?p=1510136#post1510136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadow Lords: This feels like kinda low hanging fruit because they're already the manipulative bastard Tribe and generally upset that the Silver Fangs get all the respect in the Garou Nation. Resentment is a really start to a more developed story for why one would switch sides. If you want something a bit less obvious, a Child of Bat that ends up following Bat into the Wyrm's arms instead of bringing Bat back to Gaia is a more tragic background.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of the Shadow Lords my original idea is that one of them became a senior executive at Pentex or something and then had his first change belatedly, so the Shadow Lords recruited him and used him as a pawn and as a result of that he lost much of your status, your good life in the company and that would be the reason for your revolt, but I don't know, it works, but I found it weak, would you know how to complement it with something else?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510122-bsd-experimental-pack?p=1510136#post1510136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glass Walkers: The purge of the Cyberdogs is a pretty easy option, as the BSDs would gladly welcome an unethical cybernetics expert that cares more about continuing their work than patient consent. The torment they could inflict without having to hide what they're doing from their compatriots easily reflects the Wyrm's love of twisting the tools of the Weaver into things of pain and corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked the idea, would you know what someone's mindset like that would be like?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510122-bsd-experimental-pack?p=1510136#post1510136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Get of Fenris: Again you have the purge of the Swords of Heimdall to draw on as an easy source of Fenrir that might fall to the Wyrm with something a bit more nuanced than one of the most violent and bloodthirsty Tribes repeating what the White Howlers did.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes sense, but he would have to cooperate with the others and I think the mentality of that group is very limiting, so no.<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510122-bsd-experimental-pack?p=1510136#post1510136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Children of Gaia: I don't really like the Bringers of Eternal Peace, but they're the extension of the Tribe that's a natural fit for this. Deciding that the way to fix the world is to just make the Apocalypse happen ASAP makes them ripe to fall to the Wyrm in full. Anything else is probably going to feel like an awkward fit for being in the Tribe to fall later, or just too simplistic like the number of angry Crinos-born in the Tribe as it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not exactly a fan of this group either, but they good as villains and are my way out if I don't find something better, if possible I wanted to avoid them, I prefer someone having more personal motives and Eternal Peace just seems like a cult of crazy wolfs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510122-bsd-experimental-pack?p=1510136#post1510136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fianna: A lot of overlap with the Fenrir here really; or the Red Talons via the Children of Dire and Mother's Fundamentalists. The difficulty of something that's uniquely Fianna and deeper than some of the more universal things that can drive a Garou to the Spiral is one of the detriments of the Tribe. Like my example of the Child of Bat and the Shadow Lords, the Fianna do have a lot of guilt around what happened to the White Howlers and Lion, leaving a story of seeking to help repair the past taking someone down into dark places they don't come back from and still be on the side they started on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something from centuries ago, I prefer to avoid it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510122-bsd-experimental-pack?p=1510136#post1510136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silent Striders: Like the Bone Gnawers that have a continual cannibalism problem that leads many of their members astray. The Followers of Set and the Bane Mummies represent foes that would delight in bringing a Strider to the Wyrm. For something more personal, the Striders' close link to death means one can easily be haunted by their actions quite literally, driving them towards fatalistic options after too long fighting a losing war.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is more biased toward unlife than joining the BSD, but it got me thinking, what if he lost someone important and his connection to the ghosts made him look to the Wyrm for a solution? It's still an early concept, but maybe it will work.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510122-bsd-experimental-pack?p=1510136#post1510136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stargazers: Basically the same issues as the Children of Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one is hard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510122-bsd-experimental-pack?p=1510136#post1510136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Older and Younger Brother: The &quot;we gave everyone evil Camps&quot; adds the obvious story hooks here. Both Tribes have lingering resentment over the European conquest of the Americas, and members willing to deal with the Wyrm's servants to enact some revenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this could progress to something with Wendigo, but Uktena I think needs something else.\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}